> This document outlines the expected standards of behavior for all employees, directors, and contractors of NexaTech Solutions Inc. It serves as a guide to upholding our commitment to integrity, ethical conduct, and legal compliance in all business activities.

## 1. Introduction

### 1.1. Purpose and Scope

NexaTech Solutions Inc. (the “Company”) is committed to maintaining the highest standards of business conduct and ethics. This Code of Conduct (“the Code”) reflects our core values and provides a framework for our decisions, actions, and communications. The Code applies to all employees, officers, directors, and independent contractors (collectively referred to as “personnel”) of the Company and its subsidiaries worldwide.

All personnel are expected to read, understand, and comply with this Code. Acknowledgment of this Code is a condition of employment and continued service with the Company. Failure to adhere to these standards may result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment or contract.

### 1.2. Our Core Values

Our Code is built upon the foundation of our core values: **Innovation First**, **Customer Obsession**, **Integrity & Transparency**, **Collaboration**, **Excellence**, and **Sustainability**. These values guide our interactions with each other, our customers, our partners, and our community.

## 2. Workplace Conduct and Environment

### 2.1. Professionalism and Respect

We are committed to a professional, respectful, and collaborative work environment. All personnel must treat colleagues, customers, partners, and suppliers with dignity and respect. We do not tolerate harassment, discrimination, intimidation, or any form of abusive behavior.

### 2.2. Equal Opportunity and Diversity

NexaTech is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce where all individuals have the opportunity to succeed. Employment decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and business needs, without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law.

### 2.3. Health and Safety

The safety and well-being of our personnel are paramount. We are committed to providing a safe and healthy work environment in compliance with all applicable laws and regulations. All personnel are responsible for following safety procedures, reporting accidents or unsafe conditions, and contributing to a culture of safety.

## 3. Business Integrity and Ethics

### 3.1. Anti-Corruption and Bribery

We have a zero-tolerance policy for bribery and corruption. Personnel must not offer, give, solicit, or accept bribes, kickbacks, or any other improper payments to or from any individual or entity, including government officials. All business dealings must be transparent and accurately recorded.

### 3.2. Conflicts of Interest

Personnel must avoid any situation that creates or appears to create a conflict of interest between their personal interests and the interests of the Company. A conflict of interest may arise when an individual's personal, social, financial, or political activities interfere with their loyalty and objectivity to the Company. Any potential conflicts of interest must be disclosed to the Legal Department immediately.

### 3.3. Gifts and Entertainment

The exchange of modest gifts and entertainment can be a legitimate part of business. However, such exchanges must not be intended to improperly influence business decisions. Personnel must adhere to the Company’s detailed Gifts & Entertainment Policy and exercise good judgment to ensure all exchanges are reasonable, infrequent, and in compliance with applicable laws.

## 4. Information and Asset Protection

### 4.1. Confidentiality and Data Privacy

Personnel are entrusted with confidential information belonging to the Company, our customers, and our partners. This includes trade secrets, financial data, customer lists, and personal information. All personnel have a duty to protect this information from unauthorized disclosure or use. We are committed to complying with all applicable data privacy laws, including GDPR and HIPAA.

### 4.2. Use of Company Assets

Company assets, including computer systems, software, equipment, and facilities, are provided for legitimate business purposes. Incidental personal use may be permitted but should be minimal and must not interfere with work responsibilities or violate any other Company policy. Personnel are expected to protect Company assets from loss, theft, or damage.

### 4.3. Intellectual Property

Our intellectual property, including patents, trademarks, copyrights, and trade secrets, is one of our most valuable assets. Personnel must take appropriate steps to protect the Company’s intellectual property rights. Any inventions, discoveries, or creative works developed by personnel within the scope of their employment are the exclusive property of NexaTech Solutions.

## 5. Compliance and Reporting

### 5.1. Compliance with Laws and Regulations

We are committed to conducting our business in full compliance with all applicable laws and regulations in the jurisdictions where we operate. It is the responsibility of all personnel to be aware of and comply with the laws relevant to their roles.

### 5.2. Accurate Record-Keeping

All business transactions, financial records, and reports must be accurate, complete, and timely. False or misleading entries in Company records are strictly prohibited. Our financial reporting will always be in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP) and other applicable standards.

### 5.3. Reporting Violations and Whistleblower Protection

We encourage all personnel to speak up and report any suspected violations of this Code, Company policies, or the law. Reports can be made to a manager, Human Resources, the Legal Department, or through our confidential ethics hotline. The Company strictly prohibits retaliation against any individual who reports a concern in good faith.

## 6. Conclusion

This Code of Conduct serves as a guide for ethical decision-making and professional conduct. However, no code can address every possible situation. We rely on the sound judgment and integrity of our personnel to uphold these principles in their daily work. By adhering to this Code, we protect our reputation, build trust with our stakeholders, and ensure the long-term success of NexaTech Solutions.

